### Scene Description in RDF Triples (Turtle Format)
```turtle
@prefix : <http://cecs571.csulb.edu/ontology/cornercase#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

:scene1 a :Scene ;
    :scenarioName "NighttimePedestrianAndCyclistObstructionScenario" ;
    :hasCornerCaseType :cc1 .

:cc1 a :BehaviorAnomaly ;
    :hasActor :actor1, :actor2 ;
    :hasObstacle :obstacle1, :obstacle2 ;
    :hasWeatherCondition :weather1 ;
    :hasRisk :risk1, :risk2, :risk3 .

:actor1 a :Cyclist ;
    :description "Cyclist pushing bicycle on road" .
:actor2 a :Pedestrian ;
    :description "Pedestrian walking on road" .

:obstacle1 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Large cylindrical obstacle on road" .
:obstacle2 a :RoadObject ;
    :description "Orange traffic cones on road" .

:weather1 a :NightCondition ;
    :description "Low-light nighttime conditions" .

:risk1 a :PedestrianCollisionRisk ;
    :description "Pedestrian walking into vehicle path" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev1 .
:risk2 a :CollisionRisk ;
    :description "Cyclist pushing bicycle into vehicle path" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev2 .
:risk3 a :OcclusionRisk ;
    :description "Obstacles (cylindrical object and cones) reducing visibility" ;
    :hasSeverityScore :sev3 .

:sev1 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.90"^^xsd:float .
:sev2 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.85"^^xsd:float ;
:sev3 a :SeverityScore ;
    :severityValue "0.75"^^xsd:float .
```

